.TH DEFW-PYTHON 1 "November 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
defw-python \- run Python on DEFw
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B defw-python
.I script
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B defw-python \-m
.I module
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B defw-python \-\-serve
.I module
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B defw-python
activates QFw when it is not active, locates the DEFw launcher
.B defw2-python
under
.BR DEFW_PREFIX ,
and runs it with the same arguments. The launcher runs the active Python
interpreter as a DEFw v2 process and provides the DEFw module names that QFw
code imports.
.PP
A script or a module runs as a DEFw client. With
.BR \-\-serve ,
the named QPM service module is served until it is told to stop.
.PP
Normal applications use this entry point indirectly through
.BR qfw-srun (1),
and QPM services through
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1).
It is also useful for low-level diagnostics that require a DEFw agent context.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIRTUAL_ENV
Selects the Python interpreter when it contains
.IR bin/python .
.TP
.B DEFW_PREFIX
Selects the DEFw installation. The activated QFw environment supplies the
default.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The launcher's or the application's status is returned. A missing launcher
returns 127.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-activate (1),
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw (7)
